    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "From these results, it is easy to determine the modular curves of the form X 0 ( N ) with density degree 1, 2, 3 and 4. For example, X 0 ( N ) has density degree 4 if and only if N occurs in the set of Theorem 1.8 but not in the sets of Theorems 1.6 and 1.7. Motivated by the recent work of Kadets and Vogt [23] on density degrees, we determine all curves X 0 ( N ) with density degree equal to 5. Our main result is the following theorem:"
