    "font" : "CMR12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "This main theorem is an important step in determining all curves X 0 ( N ) with inﬁnitely many quintic points. In fact, if a curve has inﬁnitely many quintic points, then it has to have density degree ≤ 5. And our result completes the classiﬁcation of all modular curves of density degree ≤ 5. So, in order to determine all curves X 0 ( N ) with inﬁnitely many quintic points, it suﬃces to determine for the explicit list X 0 ( N ) of density degree ≤ 4 whether they have inﬁnitely many quintic points. With some extra work, we are able to prove the following:"
